Following KSR, the Federal Circuit held that although "rigid" application of the TSM test for obviousness is improper, application of a flexible TSM test remains the primary guarantee against improper "hindsight" analysis, because a flexibly applied TSM test ensures that the obviousness analysis proceeds on the basis of evidence in existence before time the applicationwas filed, as required by 35 U.S.C. §  SVG
